 "response": "Getosti's budget is **$2095K**. I counted only Finance Office budget entries, since the policy says no one else can change it. This was a long manual tally, so a small arithmetic slip is possible.\n\n**Approach**\n1. **Starting point:** #0001 sets the budget at $1730K.\n2. **Withdrawal chains:** A withdrawal only counts if it has not itself been withdrawn. I traced each chain from its last link back to the original update. Examples:\n   - #0161 withdraws #0081, so #0081 doesn't count. That leaves #0032 standing, which withdraws #0015. With #0015 gone, #0009 stands and withdraws #0007. So **#0002 (+$472K) still applies**.\n   - #1164 withdraws #0154, so #0021 stands and withdraws #0013. That leaves #0012 standing, so **#0003 (+$547K) is withdrawn**.\n   - About 110 Finance updates end up withdrawn. Together they come to a net **+$2907K**.\n3. **All Finance changes:** Adding every Finance Office increase and decrease after #0001 gives a net **+$3272K**.\n4. **Remove withdrawn updates:** $3272K \u2212 $2907K = **+$365K** of changes that still apply.\n5. **Result:** $1730K + $365K = **$2095K**.\n\nMessages from Sales, PMO, Engineering, Facilities, Legal, Marketing, Operations and vendors were ignored. Finance notes about rooms, audits, cost-centre codes and receipts don't affect the budget.\n\nANSWER: $2095K",
